+## What's changed in v3
 
-Undo/Redo and workspace resizing now preflight the restored view and, when necessary, zoom closer around the same model-space center. Fit starts with the usual several-repeat view and uses the same bounded, copy-count-aware fallback. A camera that is already safe is left unchanged. The placement-list recentering fallback also uses this recovery path.
+The canvas is now framed by a 48px application bar, compact grouped document controls, a contextual selection toolbar, and narrower neutral sidebars. System sans-serif text, readable metadata, restrained borders, consistent spacing, and one selection accent replace the decorative branding. Source images use compact rows; placements have clear stacking direction and explicit flip state. Inspector comes first on the right, followed by Export and PNG verification. Export is the only filled primary action.
 
-When no view at the requested center fits within 800% zoom, an inline error is shown. An already-safe view is preserved on a failed Fit. If a history change or resize leaves the current view over budget, finite, bounded pan/zoom navigation remains available, including through still-over-limit intermediate views. Those intermediate scenes render **zero motif copies**, never a truncated scene. This lets wheel increments accumulate and lets Space-pan reach a less dense center even at maximum zoom.
+The empty state is task-oriented. Pan state, focus, destructive actions, native-size warnings, rejected edits, render-budget recovery, pending exports, proof failures, and stale proofs have distinct feedback. Settings retain their labels at narrow desktop widths; sidebars scroll independently. Desktop layouts were statically audited from **900 × 600** through **1480 × 900**. The shell has a 900px minimum width and 540px minimum height; smaller windows are outside the intended layout. No mobile interface is added.
 
-The 2000-copy cap, document/placement transforms, undo snapshots, assets, and PNG export path are unchanged. No dependencies or app features were added. Version metadata is now 2.0.0.
